  "question": {
    "text": "Let \\(f(x)=\\frac{\\left(e^x-1\\right)^2}{\\sin \\left(\\frac{x}{a}\\right) \\log \\left(1+\\frac{x}{4}\\right)}\\) for \\(x \\neq 0\\), and \\(f(0)=12\\). If \\(\\mathrm{f}\\) is continuous at \\(x=0\\), then the value of \\(a\\) is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "D6K6Q",
      "text": "1",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "bMoow",
      "text": "-1",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JuVR6",
      "text": "2",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "5Gv7r",
      "text": "3",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "\\(\\begin{aligned}\n& \\operatorname{Lt}_{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{\\left(e^x-1\\right)^2}{\\sin \\left(\\frac{x}{a}\\right) \\log \\left(1+\\frac{x}{4}\\right)} \\\\\n&=\\operatorname{Lt}_{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{\\frac{\\left(e^x-1\\right)^2}{x} \\cdot x^2}{\\frac{x}{a} \\cdot \\frac{\\sin \\left(\\frac{x}{a}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{x}{a}\\right)} \\cdot \\frac{\\log \\left(1+\\frac{x}{4}\\right)}{\\frac{x}{4}} \\cdot \\frac{x}{4}} \\Rightarrow 4 a=12 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow a=3\n\\end{aligned}\\)",
    "image": null
  },
